    thinking: "**Analyzing App Structure**\n\nI\'ve examined the app\'s structure and have pinpointed that `App.tsx` handles `activeTab` navigation. Specifically, within `renderView()`, the `DetailView` component is rendered when `activeTab` is \'detail\' and `currentItem` exists. This provides the conditional logic.\n\n\n**Identifying the Screen**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the footer in `App.tsx` and the user\'s prompt related to the `DetailView`. The lack of a direct screen ID is now apparent. I can see that the `DetailView` presents device information, but there isn\'t an explicit identifier for the screen itself, though I now can identify it based on the detail screen\'s conditional rendering in conjunction with the `App.tsx` footer. I am now rethinking how to best address this lack of clarity for the user\'s question, and seeking a method to identify this screen type.\n\n\n**Designing Developer Information**\n\nI\'m now focused on delivering an elegant solution for identifying the active screen and its corresponding source file within the app. I\'m exploring a \"Developer Diagnostics Panel\" or \"Source File Badge,\" ideally integrated within the existing footer in `App.tsx`. The idea is to dynamically display the active component\'s name and its source path. For example, the footer could show \"Active Component: DetailView (src/components/views/DetailView.tsx)\" based on the active tab/view. This avoids clutter and offers easy identification. I am now exploring the best method for dynamically displaying the correct component.\n\n\n**Mapping Component Sources**\n\nI\'ve created an index that maps view keys to component names and their corresponding source file paths. This includes components like DashboardView and YANGValidatorView. This map should be a solid foundation for identifying the active view\'s source.\n\n\n**Implementing Source Display**\n\nI\'ve formulated a streamlined approach: an informational badge in the footer. By checking `activeTab` and `currentItem`, I can now dynamically fetch the relevant source file information, using the `VIEW_SOURCE_MAP` I created. This conditional logic identifies the active source, enabling its display via a tooltip or similar interaction in the footer.\n\n\n**Refining Presentation Options**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on presentational refinements. My focus is on delivering a solution that remains elegant within the existing footer context. I am leaning towards the \"Source Inspector\" approach: `[Inspect Screen: {activeSource.name} ({activeSource.file})]`. I can also consider displaying `Active View: DetailView | /src/components/views/DetailView.tsx` with a little badge to keep the UI clean. Further, I can include console logging for added visibility.\n\n\n"
